{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>וכל הנשים</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the other two: וכל הנשים יתנו יקר, וכל הנשים העומדות — in the matter of Jeremiah, who told them to abstain from idolatry. These women who engaged in the work of the heavens — יתנו יקר; but those accursed women who burn incense to the host of the heavens caused that they were exiled and became a byword and a taunt." "<b>אותנה</b> Twice: here, and the other: עד אשר הפיצותם אותנה — in Ezekiel, in the matter of the shepherds who feed the sheep with their feet trampling. These caused the Shechinah to descend and dwell in Israel, but those evil shepherds who cause Israel to sin cause the Shechinah to withdraw from Israel."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The two additional Masorah citations appear to be from Ezekiel 24:25 and Jeremiah 44:19 respectively, but are left unaddressed as per instructions.", 1 "The Ezekiel citation appears to be from Ezekiel 34:18–19."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:09.414068161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}